# Optional per-scope packet delivery byte caps.
#
# Copy this file to packet-limits.conf to opt in. Scope names must already
# exist in projects.txt. Use either a tab or "=" between the scope and byte
# limit. Unlisted scopes keep the 14,000-byte default; values below 4,000 are
# clamped to 4,000. The cap covers complete spine-packet output, including
# delta/recent sections; base packets normally reserve bounded dynamic room,
# but protected pins may consume that reserve.
# Pins are never dropped, so generation fails if all pins cannot fit. Invalid
# entries warn by line number and are ignored.
#
# Non-ASCII packet text often uses multiple UTF-8 bytes per character, so two
# scopes with the same record count can need different byte caps.
#
# research=20000
# work	18000
